IMPORT prelude

-- Building (Strata Management) Act 2004 (Singapore; enacted as the Building Maintenance and Strata Management Act) -- what the
-- owner of a strata lot faces: what an improvement to my lot needs and whether I can be made to undo one (ss 37, 37A, 30, 111);
-- what by-laws can and cannot control (s 32(3), (9)); my share of the contributions, interest, the written demand and the
-- offence of not paying (ss 40, 41(1), (2)); buying a lot with arrears on it (ss 40(3), (4), 47); the charge on my lot and the
-- management corporation's power to sell it (s 43); my guarantee of the management corporation's debts (s 44); whether I may
-- vote (First Schedule para 2, s 65(9)), stand for the council or be removed from it (ss 53, 54); the duties I owe my neighbours
-- (s 63); when the management corporation may enter my lot (s 31); notifying my sale (s 65(2)); and what I can be fined.
--
-- SEAT: the subsidiary proprietor -- the owner -- of a lot in a strata development (and, for s 63, anyone who occupies the
-- lot). Every decision is phrased as that person would ask it.
--
-- Provisions covered: s 30(2), (3); s 31(1), (2); s 32(3), (9); s 37(1) to (4A); s 37A; s 40(2) to (4), (6)(b), (9), (10);
-- s 41(1), (2); s 43(1), (3), (5); s 44; s 47(1)(c), (2), (3); s 48(1A); s 53(6), (7), (8)(a), (9), (9B), (12); s 54(1)(c),
-- (2)(a); s 63; s 65(2), (8), (9); s 111(b); s 120(2); s 128; First Schedule para 2(1)(a), (2).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, version in force from 1 October 2026 (amendments to Act 15 of 2026
-- shown, some in force 1 July and 1 October 2026), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/BSMA2004.txt. The deposit's
-- arrangement of sections is out of step with the body; the encoding follows the body's section numbers.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the schedule of strata units and developer management (Parts 4 and 5 Division 1); the management corporation's
-- own duties, funds, accounts and records except where they reach the owner; meetings and resolutions (s 2(2) to (8), the First
-- Schedule beyond para 2); exclusive-use by-laws (s 33) and common-property leases (ss 34, 34A); insurance; subsidiary
-- management corporations; managing agents; the Strata Titles Boards' constitution and procedure, and their orders other than
-- s 111(b); additional and varied contributions under ss 41(3), (6), (8) and 108(3) (where one applies the share answers
-- NOTHING); the Commissioner's powers; regulations (s 136), commencement and transitional provisions. No regulations or
-- prescribed by-laws were deposited; "floor area" (s 37(5), rule 2 of the Planning (Development) Rules 2008) is asked as a fact.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the
-- individual to whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Building (Strata Management) Act 2004 -- the owner of a lot`

-- "subsidiary proprietor": the owner of a lot (a flat, shop or other unit) in a strata title plan.
-- "management corporation": the body of all the owners, which runs the common property and levies contributions.
-- "share value": the number given to my lot in the schedule of strata units; s 62(1) it fixes my votes, my share of the common
-- property and (subject to ss 41 and 108(3)) my contributions.

§§ `37, 37A, 111 -- improving my lot`

-- s 37(1): "a subsidiary proprietor ... must not effect any improvement in or upon the lot for the subsidiary proprietor's benefit
-- which increases or is likely to increase the floor area" except under an authority given under (2): "by 90% resolution".
-- (2A): that does not affect the Planning Act 1998 or any requirement under it "for written permission".
-- s 37(3): "Except pursuant to an authority granted under subsection (4) by the management corporation or permitted under
-- section 37A", I must not effect "any other improvement ... which affects the appearance of any building".
-- s 37A(1): I "may install safety equipment on the lot, or as part of any window, door or opening on the lot which is facing
-- outdoors, despite any other provision of this Act or the regulations or any by-law of the parcel which otherwise prohibits"
-- it. s 37A(3) "safety equipment": (a) to prevent falls over an outdoor-facing balcony, terrace, window, door or opening --
-- (i) a window grille or screen, (ii) a balustrade, railing or fence; (b) a device restricting the opening of an outdoor-facing
-- window, door or opening; (c) a screen or device to prevent entry of animals or insects; (d) an intruder alarm or monitoring
-- system; (e) a lock or other security mechanism protecting occupiers against intruders.

DECLARE `What I want to install` IS ONE OF
    `a window grille or screen against falls`
    -- s 37A(3)(a)(i)
    `a balustrade, railing or fence against falls`
    -- s 37A(3)(a)(ii)
    `a window or door restrictor`
    -- s 37A(3)(b)
    `a screen against animals or insects`
    -- s 37A(3)(c): the "cat mesh"
    `an intruder alarm or monitoring system`
    -- s 37A(3)(d)
    `a lock or security mechanism against intruders`
    -- s 37A(3)(e)
    `something that is not safety equipment`
    -- anything else: an enclosure, an awning, new windows, re-tiling

DECLARE `My improvement` HAS
    `what it is`                                         IS A `What I want to install`
    `it increases or is likely to increase the floor area` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- "floor area" as in rule 2 of the Planning (Development) Rules 2008 (s 37(5)); asked as a fact
    `it affects the appearance of the building`          IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the improvement` IS A `My improvement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is it safety equipment under section 37A` IF
    CONSIDER `the improvement`'s `what it is`
    WHEN `something that is not safety equipment` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

DECLARE `What my improvement needs` IS ONE OF
    `a 90% resolution authorising it, and planning permission if the Planning Act requires it`
    -- s 37(1), (2), (2A)
    `the management corporation's authority under section 37(4)`
    -- s 37(3), (4)
    `no authority: section 37A permits it despite any by-law`
    -- s 37A(1), on the conditions in s 37A(2)
    `no authority under section 37`
    -- neither floor area nor appearance is affected

-- Inference, labelled: s 37A(1) operates "despite any other provision of this Act", so it is read as overriding s 37(1) as well
-- as s 37(3), which names it expressly. Safety equipment is therefore tested first.
GIVEN `the improvement` IS A `My improvement`
GIVETH A `What my improvement needs`
DECIDE `What do I need before I make this improvement` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `Is it safety equipment under section 37A` `the improvement`
            THEN `no authority: section 37A permits it despite any by-law`
        IF `the improvement`'s `it increases or is likely to increase the floor area`
            THEN `a 90% resolution authorising it, and planning permission if the Planning Act requires it`
        IF `the improvement`'s `it affects the appearance of the building`
            THEN `the management corporation's authority under section 37(4)`
        OTHERWISE `no authority under section 37`

-- s 37A(2): a subsidiary proprietor who installs safety equipment "must -- (a) repair any damage caused to any part of the common
-- property or limited common property ... by the installation ...; and (b) ensure that the safety equipment is installed in a
-- competent and proper manner and has an appearance, after it has been installed, in keeping with the appearance of the
-- building".
GIVEN `I repaired any damage to the common property`          IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was installed in a competent and proper manner`     IS A BOOLEAN
      `its appearance is in keeping with the building`        IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I met my duties in installing safety equipment` IF
        `I repaired any damage to the common property`
    AND `it was installed in a competent and proper manner`
    AND `its appearance is in keeping with the building`

-- s 37(4): the management corporation "may ... authorise" an appearance improvement "if the management corporation is satisfied
-- that the improvement ... (a) will not detract from the appearance of any of the buildings ... or will be in keeping with the
-- rest of the buildings; and (b) will not affect the structural integrity of any of the buildings". Its satisfaction is its own
-- judgment: asked as an input, never guessed. Even when satisfied it "may", not must.
GIVEN `the management corporation is satisfied it will not detract from the appearance or is in keeping` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the management corporation is satisfied it will not affect structural integrity`              IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the management corporation authorise my improvement under section 37(4)` IF
        `the management corporation is satisfied it will not detract from the appearance or is in keeping`
    AND `the management corporation is satisfied it will not affect structural integrity`

-- s 111(b): on my application, if a Board "considers that the management corporation ... has unreasonably refused to authorise
-- under section 37(4) any improvement ... which affects the appearance of any building", it may order the management corporation
-- to consent. Only an appearance improvement under s 37(4) is within (b); a floor-area improvement needs a 90% resolution and is
-- not. Whether the refusal was unreasonable is the Board's judgment, asked as an input.
GIVEN `the improvement`                                         IS A `My improvement`
      `the management corporation refused to authorise it`     IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Board considers the refusal unreasonable`           IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can a Board order the management corporation to consent to my improvement` IF
        `What do I need before I make this improvement` `the improvement`
            EQUALS `the management corporation's authority under section 37(4)`
    AND `the management corporation refused to authorise it`
    AND `the Board considers the refusal unreasonable`

-- s 37(4A): where the management corporation "is satisfied that an improvement ... is effected in contravention of subsection (1)
-- or (3)", it may by written notice "given to the subsidiary proprietor of the lot (whether or not the subsidiary proprietor is
-- responsible for the contravention)" require me to carry out "at the subsidiary proprietor's own cost" works to remedy the breach
-- "within a reasonable time specified in the notice".
-- s 30(2)(a), (d), (3): if I fail to carry out work required by a s 37(4A) notice or to rectify my contravention of s 37(1) or (3),
-- the management corporation may carry it out and recover the cost "as a debt", from me or (s 30(3)(b)(ii)) from anyone who
-- later becomes the subsidiary proprietor of the lot "in respect of which ... the notice under section 37(4A) was given".
GIVEN `I am the subsidiary proprietor now`                                    IS A BOOLEAN
      `the management corporation is satisfied the improvement contravened section 37(1) or (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be made to undo an unauthorised improvement at my own cost` IF
        `I am the subsidiary proprietor now`
    AND `the management corporation is satisfied the improvement contravened section 37(1) or (3)`

GIVEN `a section 37(4A) notice was given for my lot`   IS A BOOLEAN
      `the required work was not done`                 IS A BOOLEAN
      `the management corporation carried out the work` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the management corporation recover from me the cost of remedial work it did` IF
        `a section 37(4A) notice was given for my lot`
    AND `the required work was not done`
    AND `the management corporation carried out the work`

§§ `32 -- what by-laws can control`

-- s 32(3): by special resolution the management corporation may make by-laws "for the purpose of controlling and managing the use
-- or enjoyment of the parcel", including "(c) the keeping of pets; (d) parking; (e) floor coverings".
-- s 32(9): "No by-law made under this section or section 33 is capable of operating -- (a) to prohibit or restrict the devolution
-- of a lot or a transfer, lease, mortgage or other dealing of a lot". s 32(12): "lease" includes a tenancy agreement.
-- s 37A(1): safety equipment may be installed despite "any by-law of the parcel which otherwise prohibits" it.
DECLARE `What I want to do with my lot` IS ONE OF
    `let it out on a tenancy`
    `sell it`
    `mortgage it`
    `leave it by will`
    -- "devolution"
    `keep a pet`
    `park in the common car park`
    `lay a new floor covering`
    `install a window grille`

GIVEN `what` IS A `What I want to do with my lot`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can a by-law stop or restrict me doing this` IF
    CONSIDER `what`
    WHEN `let it out on a tenancy`      THEN FALSE
    WHEN `sell it`                      THEN FALSE
    WHEN `mortgage it`                  THEN FALSE
    WHEN `leave it by will`             THEN FALSE
    WHEN `install a window grille`      THEN FALSE
    WHEN `keep a pet`                   THEN TRUE
    WHEN `park in the common car park`  THEN TRUE
    WHEN `lay a new floor covering`     THEN TRUE

§§ `40, 41 -- my contributions`

-- s 40(2): "Subject to sections 41 and 108(3), the contributions levied ... in respect of each lot are payable by the subsidiary
-- proprietors in shares proportional to the share value of their respective lots".
-- s 41(1): "Despite section 40(2), the contributions payable by the subsidiary proprietor of a proposed lot are, during the period
-- when any building consisting of that proposed lot is being erected and is not yet completed, reduced by 75%."
-- (2): the building "is deemed to be completed when a temporary occupation permit is issued for any proposed lot in the
-- building".
-- Other methods -- additional contributions approved by the Commissioner (s 41(3), (4)), a comprehensive resolution (s 41(6)),
-- a resolution by consensus (s 41(8)), a Board's variation (s 108(3)) -- are not encoded: the share answers NOTHING.

DECLARE `My levy` HAS
    `the total contributions levied`                                IS A NUMBER
    -- dollars, for all lots together
    `my share value`                                                IS A NUMBER
    `the aggregate share value`                                     IS A NUMBER
    `my lot is a proposed lot in a building still being erected`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `a temporary occupation permit has been issued for any proposed lot in the building` IS A BOOLEAN
    `another method applies under section 41(3), (6), (8) or 108(3)` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the levy` IS A `My levy`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my contribution reduced by 75% under section 41` IF
        `the levy`'s `my lot is a proposed lot in a building still being erected`
    AND NOT `the levy`'s `a temporary occupation permit has been issued for any proposed lot in the building`

GIVEN `the levy` IS A `My levy`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my share of the contributions` IS
    IF `the levy`'s `another method applies under section 41(3), (6), (8) or 108(3)`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `Is my contribution reduced by 75% under section 41` `the levy`
         THEN JUST (`proportional share` TIMES 25%)
         ELSE JUST `proportional share`
    WHERE
        `proportional share` MEANS
            `the levy`'s `the total contributions levied` TIMES `the levy`'s `my share value`
                DIVIDED BY `the levy`'s `the aggregate share value`

-- s 40(6)(b): a contribution "if not paid on or before the 30th day after it becomes due and payable, bears interest at the rate
-- determined by the management corporation and the interest accrues from the expiry of 30 days after the date when the
-- contribution becomes due and payable unless the management corporation determines in a general meeting ... that any unpaid
-- contribution bears no interest".
-- s 40(9): where it "is not paid on or before the 30th day after it becomes due and payable, the management corporation may serve
-- a written demand".
-- Counting: day 1 is the day after the due date; paid on day 30 is in time; interest and a demand are possible from day 31.
GIVEN `days since it became due, still unpaid`                      IS A NUMBER
      `the general meeting determined it bears no interest`         IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my unpaid contribution bear interest` IF
        `days since it became due, still unpaid` GREATER THAN 30
    AND NOT `the general meeting determined it bears no interest`

GIVEN `days since it became due, still unpaid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can a written demand be served on me` IF
    `days since it became due, still unpaid` GREATER THAN 30

-- s 40(10): "A subsidiary proprietor who fails to pay any contribution or interest due and owing ... before the 14th day after the
-- date of service of any written demand mentioned in subsection (9) shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on
-- conviction to a fine not exceeding $10,000 and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not exceeding $100 for
-- every day or part of a day during which the contribution or interest or both remain unpaid after conviction."
-- "before the 14th day": payment on the 13th day after service is in time; on the 14th it is not.
-- s 40(11): the court may also order me to pay the contribution and interest, recoverable as a fine.
GIVEN `a written demand was served on me`              IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day after service on which I paid`          IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      -- NOTHING if I have not paid
      `days since service`                             IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I committed the offence of not paying after a written demand` IF
        `a written demand was served on me`
    AND `days since service` AT LEAST 14
    AND `I did not pay before the 14th day`
    WHERE
        `I did not pay before the 14th day` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the day after service on which I paid`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
            WHEN JUST d  THEN d AT LEAST 14

-- The duty behind s 40(10), as a regulative rule counted in days from service: pay within 13 days.
DECLARE `Owner` IS ONE OF `I, the subsidiary proprietor`
DECLARE `Owner's step` IS ONE OF
    `pay the contribution and interest demanded`
    `give the management corporation written notice of the transfer`

`my duty to pay after a written demand` MEANS
    PARTY `I, the subsidiary proprietor`
    MUST `pay the contribution and interest demanded`
    WITHIN 13
    LEST BREACH BY `I, the subsidiary proprietor`

§§ `40(3), (4), 47 -- buying or selling a lot with arrears`

-- s 40(3): "If, at the time a person becomes a subsidiary proprietor of a lot, another person is liable in respect of the lot to
-- pay a contribution ..., the subsidiary proprietor shall, subject to section 47(3), be jointly and severally liable with the
-- other person for the payment of the contribution and interest".
-- s 47(3): "In favour of a donee of, or a person taking for valuable consideration, an estate or interest in any lot, a certificate
-- given under subsection (1)(c) ... is conclusive evidence, as at the date of the certificate, of the matters stated therein."
-- Inference, labelled: "subject to section 47(3)" is read as protecting a buyer whose s 47(1)(c) certificate stated that nothing
-- was unpaid; the encoding does not apportion arrears levied between the certificate's date and the purchase.
GIVEN `contributions on the lot were unpaid when I became the subsidiary proprietor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I relied on a section 47 certificate stating nothing was unpaid`             IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As the buyer, am I liable with the seller for the arrears` IF
        `contributions on the lot were unpaid when I became the subsidiary proprietor`
    AND NOT `I relied on a section 47 certificate stating nothing was unpaid`

-- s 40(4): "A person who has ceased to be a subsidiary proprietor of the lot is only liable to pay the contribution ... which was
-- unpaid at the time the person ceased to be a subsidiary proprietor, plus the interest accruing on the unpaid contribution until
-- the time it is paid."
GIVEN `the contribution was levied and unpaid before I ceased to be the subsidiary proprietor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As the seller, am I still liable for this contribution` IF
    `the contribution was levied and unpaid before I ceased to be the subsidiary proprietor`

-- s 47(1)(c): on written application by a subsidiary proprietor, mortgagee or prospective purchaser and payment of the
-- prescribed fee, the management corporation must certify the regular contributions, any unpaid contributions, any s 30 amount
-- and any interest. (2): if no time for inspection under (1)(b) is agreed "on or before the 7th day after the receipt of the
-- application", the management corporation must fix a time "being a date not later than the 21st day after the receipt".
GIVEN `a time for inspection was agreed on or before the 7th day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `By which day after my application must I be allowed to inspect` IS
    IF `a time for inspection was agreed on or before the 7th day`
    THEN NOTHING
    -- the agreed time governs; the Act fixes no day
    ELSE JUST 21

§§ `43 -- the charge on my lot and the power of sale`

-- s 43(1): where an amount recoverable under s 30, or a contribution levied under s 40 or 41, "remains unpaid on the expiry of a
-- period of 30 days after the management corporation has served a written demand", it, with interest, "constitutes a charge on
-- the lot ... upon lodgment of an instrument of charge ... and the registration thereof by the Registrar of Titles".
-- (2): the management corporation then has "the power of sale ... as if the management corporation is a registered mortgagee".
-- (3): it "must not proceed to sell the lot ... unless -- (a) a special resolution has been passed ... to have the lot sold;
-- (b) a notice of the intended sale has been published once in one or more daily newspapers approved by the Registrar of Titles;
-- (c) during the period of 6 weeks after the date of such publication, no payment has been received for the amount or
-- contribution due (including interest thereon) and the cost of publication ... as well as any other necessary incidental
-- charges; and (d) there is no legal action pending in court to restrain the management corporation from proceeding with the
-- sale."
-- (5): if I pay "the whole amount or contribution due (including interest thereon) and any necessary or incidental charges
-- (including legal costs) ... before it has exercised its power of sale", I am entitled to an instrument of discharge.
-- Counting: the 30 days and the 6 weeks (42 days) are complete at the end of their last day; the step is open from the next day.

DECLARE `My arrears` HAS
    `days since the written demand was served`        IS A NUMBER
    `still unpaid`                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `an instrument of charge has been registered`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `a special resolution to sell has been passed`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `notice of the sale has been published in an approved daily newspaper` IS A BOOLEAN
    `days since publication`                          IS A NUMBER
    `I paid everything due, with the publication cost and charges, after publication` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a court action to restrain the sale is pending`  IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the arrears` IS A `My arrears`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my arrears become a charge on my lot` IF
        `the arrears`'s `still unpaid`
    AND `the arrears`'s `days since the written demand was served` GREATER THAN 30

GIVEN `the arrears` IS A `My arrears`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the management corporation sell my lot` IF
        `the arrears`'s `an instrument of charge has been registered`
    AND `the arrears`'s `a special resolution to sell has been passed`
    AND `the arrears`'s `notice of the sale has been published in an approved daily newspaper`
    AND `the arrears`'s `days since publication` GREATER THAN 42
    AND NOT `the arrears`'s `I paid everything due, with the publication cost and charges, after publication`
    AND NOT `the arrears`'s `a court action to restrain the sale is pending`

GIVEN `I paid the whole amount, interest and charges including legal costs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the management corporation has already exercised its power of sale`   IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to a discharge of the charge` IF
        `I paid the whole amount, interest and charges including legal costs`
    AND NOT `the management corporation has already exercised its power of sale`

§§ `44 -- my guarantee of the management corporation's debts`

-- s 44(1): "The payment of any expenditure lawfully incurred by a management corporation ... is ... guaranteed by the persons who,
-- for the time being and from time to time, comprise the management corporation." (2): "The subsidiary proprietor of a lot is
-- liable only to pay the amount which the subsidiary proprietor would have to pay if contributions were levied ... under section
-- 40 or 41(6) to raise the necessary sum". The s 40(2) formula (share value) is used; a s 41(6) formula is not encoded.
-- Expenditure not lawfully incurred is outside s 44: my guarantee of it under s 44 is nil.
GIVEN `the expenditure`                IS A NUMBER
      `it was lawfully incurred`       IS A BOOLEAN
      `my share value`                 IS A NUMBER
      `the aggregate share value`      IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be made to pay on the management corporation's debt` IS
    IF `it was lawfully incurred`
    THEN `the expenditure` TIMES `my share value` DIVIDED BY `the aggregate share value`
    ELSE 0

§§ `First Schedule para 2, 65(9) -- may I vote`

-- First Schedule para 2(1)(a): a person may vote in respect of a lot "only if ... the person is the subsidiary proprietor or a
-- mortgagee in possession or a receiver of that lot as shown on the strata roll and has paid to the management corporation all
-- contributions and any other moneys levied or recoverable".
-- para 2(2): a first mortgagee shown on the strata roll may vote "and, if the first mortgagee votes on that proposal, any vote
-- cast by the subsidiary proprietor of that lot on the proposal must not be counted".
-- s 65(9): a person who has not complied with a notice served under s 65(8) "is not entitled to cast a vote at any general meeting
-- ... until that person has complied".
GIVEN `I am shown on the strata roll as the subsidiary proprietor`        IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have paid all contributions and other moneys levied`             IS A BOOLEAN
      `the first mortgagee votes on the same proposal`                    IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have not complied with a section 65(8) notice served on me`      IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will my vote at the general meeting count` IF
        `I am shown on the strata roll as the subsidiary proprietor`
    AND `I have paid all contributions and other moneys levied`
    AND NOT `the first mortgagee votes on the same proposal`
    AND NOT `I have not complied with a section 65(8) notice served on me`

§§ `53, 54 -- the council`

-- s 53(6): "A person is ineligible for election as a member of the council ... unless he or she is an individual of at least
-- 21 years of age and who -- (a) is a subsidiary proprietor of a lot; (b) is nominated for election by a subsidiary proprietor of
-- a lot which is a company; or (c) is not a subsidiary proprietor but is a member of the immediate family of a subsidiary
-- proprietor and is nominated for election by that subsidiary proprietor."
-- (7): ineligible if, "on the 3rd day before the date of election", all or any part of the contributions and other moneys on the
-- lot concerned "are in arrears".
-- (8)(a): ineligible "an individual who is a joint subsidiary proprietor of a lot with another subsidiary proprietor, if that
-- other subsidiary proprietor is also a candidate at that election or has nominated another person for that election".
-- (9): "an undischarged bankrupt is eligible ... if, and only if, his or her status as an undischarged bankrupt is declared in
-- writing ... at the time of his or her nomination".
-- (8)(b), (12) (nominees of an owner of 2 or more lots beyond the threshold number) and (9A), (9B) (offices) are separate
-- rules below or not encoded.

DECLARE `How I come to the election` IS ONE OF
    `as a subsidiary proprietor`
    `as the nominee of a company that is a subsidiary proprietor`
    `as immediate family nominated by the subsidiary proprietor`
    `in none of those ways`

DECLARE `My candidacy` HAS
    `my age`                                                   IS A NUMBER
    `how I come`                                               IS A `How I come to the election`
    `the lot was in arrears on the 3rd day before the election` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my joint proprietor is also a candidate or has nominated someone` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am an undischarged bankrupt`                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `my bankruptcy was declared in writing at my nomination`   IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the candidacy` IS A `My candidacy`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I stand for election to the council` IF
        `the candidacy`'s `my age` AT LEAST 21
    AND `I come in one of the three ways`
    AND NOT `the candidacy`'s `the lot was in arrears on the 3rd day before the election`
    AND NOT (    `the candidacy`'s `how I come` EQUALS `as a subsidiary proprietor`
             AND `the candidacy`'s `my joint proprietor is also a candidate or has nominated someone`)
    AND (    NOT `the candidacy`'s `I am an undischarged bankrupt`
         OR  `the candidacy`'s `my bankruptcy was declared in writing at my nomination`)
    WHERE
        `I come in one of the three ways` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the candidacy`'s `how I come`
            WHEN `in none of those ways` THEN FALSE
            OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 53(12): "the threshold number for that subsidiary proprietor is -- (a) the number of council members that is proportional to
-- the subsidiary proprietor's share value, ignoring any fraction; or (b) 49% of the number of council members determined under
-- subsection (1), ignoring any fraction, whichever number is lower." (8)(b): my nominees beyond that number are ineligible.
GIVEN `my share value`            IS A NUMBER
      `the aggregate share value` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of council members` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many of my nominees can sit on the council` IS
    minimum (LIST (TRUNC (`the number of council members` TIMES `my share value` DIVIDED BY `the aggregate share value`) 0),
                  (TRUNC (`the number of council members` TIMES 49%) 0))

-- s 53(9B): "a person is ineligible for election or re-election to office as a treasurer ... if the re-election would result in
-- the person holding office as a treasurer for 3 consecutive terms".
GIVEN `consecutive terms I have just served as treasurer` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be re-elected as treasurer` IF
    `consecutive terms I have just served as treasurer` LESS THAN 2

-- s 54(1)(c): a member "must vacate his or her office ... if the person fails to attend 3 consecutive meetings of the council
-- without having first obtained from the council permission".
GIVEN `consecutive council meetings I missed without permission` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I lost my council seat for missing meetings` IF
    `consecutive council meetings I missed without permission` AT LEAST 3

-- s 54(2)(a): the management corporation may remove a member "without a general meeting" if all or any part of the contributions
-- or other moneys on the member's lot (or the nominating subsidiary proprietor's lot) "are in arrears for more than 3 months".
-- (b): in any other case, only "by ordinary resolution at a general meeting".
GIVEN `months my lot's contributions have been in arrears` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be removed from the council without a general meeting` IF
    `months my lot's contributions have been in arrears` GREATER THAN 3

§§ `63 -- what I owe my neighbours`

-- s 63: "A subsidiary proprietor, mortgagee in possession (whether personally or by any other person), lessee or occupier of a lot
-- must not -- (a) do anything or permit anything to be done ... so that -- (i) any support or shelter provided by that lot for
-- another lot or common property is interfered with; or (ii) the passage or provision of water, sewerage, drainage, gas,
-- electricity, garbage, artificially heated or cooled air and other services ... through ... any pipe, wire, cable or duct ... is
-- interfered with; (b) use or enjoy that lot ... so as to cause a nuisance or hazard to the occupier of any other lot ...;
-- (c) use or enjoy the common property ... so as to interfere unreasonably with the use or enjoyment of the common property by the
-- occupier of any other lot ...; or (d) use or enjoy the common property ... so as to interfere unreasonably with the use or
-- enjoyment of any other lot".
-- s 30(2)(b): if a person fails to carry out work needed to remedy a breach of s 63(a), the management corporation may do it and
-- (s 30(3)) recover the cost from that person as a debt.

DECLARE `Who I am in relation to the lot` IS ONE OF
    `the subsidiary proprietor`
    `a mortgagee in possession`
    `a lessee or tenant`
    `an occupier`
    `a visitor who does not occupy the lot`

GIVEN `who` IS A `Who I am in relation to the lot`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 63 bind me` IF
    CONSIDER `who`
    WHEN `a visitor who does not occupy the lot` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE
-- A visitor is not named in s 63; whether a particular visitor is an "occupier" is a question of fact, read here as no.

DECLARE `What I am doing` HAS
    `it interferes with support or shelter for another lot or the common property` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it interferes with services through a pipe, wire, cable or duct in my lot`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `my use of my lot causes a nuisance or hazard to another occupier`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `my use of the common property unreasonably interferes with others' use of it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my use of the common property unreasonably interferes with another lot`       IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `who`  IS A `Who I am in relation to the lot`
      `what` IS A `What I am doing`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I in breach of section 63` IF
        `Does section 63 bind me` `who`
    AND (   `what`'s `it interferes with support or shelter for another lot or the common property`
         OR `what`'s `it interferes with services through a pipe, wire, cable or duct in my lot`
         OR `what`'s `my use of my lot causes a nuisance or hazard to another occupier`
         OR `what`'s `my use of the common property unreasonably interferes with others' use of it`
         OR `what`'s `my use of the common property unreasonably interferes with another lot`)

§§ `31 -- entry into my lot`

-- s 31(1): for (a) work under s 30(1), (2), (4) or (5); (b) work required of the management corporation by a public authority's
-- notice or a Board's order; (c) work under s 29(1)(b) or (d); or (d) work to repair or renew a pipe, wire, cable or duct in
-- s 63(a)(ii), the management corporation "may, by its agents, employees or contractors, enter upon any part of the parcel ...
-- (e) in the case of an emergency -- at any time; or (f) in any other case -- at any reasonable time on notice being given to any
-- occupier of that part of the parcel."

DECLARE `Why they want to come in` IS ONE OF
    `to do work under section 30`
    `to do work a public authority or a Board requires of the management corporation`
    `to do maintenance or renewal work under section 29(1)(b) or (d)`
    `to repair or renew a service pipe, wire, cable or duct`
    `for some other purpose`

DECLARE `When they may enter` IS ONE OF
    `at any time`
    `at any reasonable time, after notice to the occupier`
    `section 31 gives no right of entry`

GIVEN `why`                     IS A `Why they want to come in`
      `it is an emergency`      IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `When they may enter`
DECIDE `When may the management corporation enter my lot` IS
    CONSIDER `why`
    WHEN `for some other purpose` THEN `section 31 gives no right of entry`
    OTHERWISE
        IF `it is an emergency`
        THEN `at any time`
        ELSE `at any reasonable time, after notice to the occupier`

§§ `65(2) -- telling the management corporation I have sold`

-- s 65(2): on the transfer of my lot on completion of a sale (or by gift), "the registered subsidiary proprietor must, not later
-- than the 10th day after the date that the instrument of transfer is registered under the Land Titles Act 1993, give to the
-- management corporation written notice of the transfer", identifying the lot, the transferee's full name and address for
-- service and the date of registration, certified by the transferee or the transferee's solicitor.
-- (8), (9): the management corporation may serve a notice requiring it within 14 days; a person who does not comply cannot vote.
-- No penalty is expressly attached to s 65(2) itself.
GIVEN `days after registration of the transfer when I gave notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did I notify my sale in time` IF
    `days after registration of the transfer when I gave notice` AT MOST 10

`my duty to notify the transfer` MEANS
    PARTY `I, the subsidiary proprietor`
    MUST `give the management corporation written notice of the transfer`
    WITHIN 10
    LEST BREACH BY `I, the subsidiary proprietor`

§§ `31(2), 40(10), 48(1A), 120(2), 128 -- what I can be fined`

-- s 40(10): fine up to $10,000, and up to $100 for every day or part of a day unpaid after conviction.
-- s 31(2): "Any person who obstructs or hinders a management corporation in the exercise of any power under this section shall be
-- guilty of an offence"; no penalty is expressly provided, so s 128: "a fine not exceeding $10,000".
-- s 48(1A): a person who, without reasonable excuse, does not deliver the management corporation's records, books, keys, strata
-- roll or other property within 7 days of notice of a council resolution: "a fine not exceeding $5,000".
-- s 120(2): "A person who contravenes any order (including an interim order) made under this Part [by a Board] ... shall be
-- liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $10,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 5 years or to both."

DECLARE `My offence` IS ONE OF
    `not paying contributions after a written demand`
    `obstructing the management corporation's entry`
    `not handing over the management corporation's records or keys`
    `disobeying a Strata Titles Board order`

DECLARE `Penalty` HAS
    `maximum fine`                          IS A NUMBER
    -- dollars
    `maximum imprisonment in months`        IS A NUMBER
    `further fine per day unpaid after conviction` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the offence` IS A `My offence`
GIVETH A `Penalty`
DECIDE `What is the most I can be punished with` IS
    --                                                                      fine,    months, per day
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `not paying contributions after a written demand`               THEN `Penalty` OF 10_000, 0,  100
    WHEN `obstructing the management corporation's entry`                THEN `Penalty` OF 10_000, 0,  0
    WHEN `not handing over the management corporation's records or keys` THEN `Penalty` OF 5_000,  0,  0
    WHEN `disobeying a Strata Titles Board order`                        THEN `Penalty` OF 10_000, 60, 0

GIVEN `days or part days still unpaid after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be fined for not paying after a written demand` IS
    10_000 PLUS 100 TIMES `days or part days still unpaid after conviction`
